  "_id": "tg-declare",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "my name may be declared throughout all the earth, Ex. 9:16 (Rom. 9:17). began Moses to declare this law, Deut. 1:5. Declare his glory among the heathen, 1 Chr. 16:24 (Ps. 96:3). declare among the people his doings, Ps. 9:11. heavens declare the glory of God, Ps. 19:1. declare thy name unto my brethren, Ps. 22:22 (Heb. 2:12). declare his righteousness unto a people, Ps. 22:31. I will declare mine iniquity, Ps. 38:18. have declared thy faithfulness and thy salvation, Ps. 40:10. heavens shall declare his righteousness, Ps. 50:6 (97:6; Isa. 57:12). watchman, let him declare what he seeth, Isa. 21:6. Who hath declared from the beginning, Isa. 41:26. I declare things that are right, Isa. 45:19. Declaring the end from the beginning, Isa. 46:10. have declared the former things from the beginning, Isa. 48:3. who shall declare his generation, Isa. 53:8 (Acts 8:33). they shall declare my glory among the Gentiles, Isa. 66:19. declareth unto man what is his thought, Amos 4:13.",
